  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Alcoholic&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KOH</mi></math>&nbsp;shows elimination reaction. In which nucleophile shows anti elimination reaction and base removes bromide ion as leaving group to form terminal alkyne.</p><p>Terminal alkyne&nbsp;has acidic hydrogen and behaves as acid.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e79d1fba-40b1-45c1-92b0-b86232b870ff-image.png\" style=\"width: 651px; height: 123px;\" /></p><p><img height=\"70\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/b70f67d4-0fdb-408c-96c2-fb64f3579450-image.png\" width=\"591\" /></p>",
